{"uid":"940e28ab9677dd62","name":"test_customer_session_persistence[webkit-with-remember-me]","fullName":"tests.ui.tests.auth.test_customer_session_security#test_customer_session_persistence","historyId":"7c649869011112288313188c4a53e9f4","time":{"start":1793738960615,"stop":1793738963060,"duration":2445},"description":"\nCheck whether “Remember Me” keeps a customer logged in after a browser restart.\n\nThe test first creates a temporary customer through the API and logs in.\nIt then closes the browser and opens it again with the same saved browser\nprofile. Reusing that profile lets the test check whether WooCommerce saved\nthe login information, as it would in a real browser.\n\nA regular ``page`` fixture gives each test a fresh, temporary browser\nsession. This test needs to close and reopen the same saved profile, so it\ncreates persistent browser sessions directly. ``trace_custom_context``\nrecords a Playwright trace for those sessions when tracing is enabled.\n\nExpected result:\n    - If Remember Me is off, the customer is logged out after restart.\n    - If Remember Me is on, the customer stays logged in after restart.\n\nArgs:\n    browser_type: Browser engine selected for this test (Chromium, Firefox,\n        or WebKit).\n    ui_base_url: Address of the storefront being tested.\n    dynamic_customer: Temporary customer account created for this test.\n        The API fixture also arranges cleanup after the test.\n    remember_me: Whether this run checks the Remember Me option.\n    trace_custom_context: Helper that saves traces for failed custom\n        browser sessions when ``--tracing retain-on-failure`` is enabled.\n\n","descriptionHtml":"<p>Check whether “Remember Me” keeps a customer logged in after a browser restart.</p>\n<p>The test first creates a temporary customer through the API and logs in.<br />\nIt then closes the browser and opens it again with the same saved browser<br />\nprofile. Reusing that profile lets the test check whether WooCommerce saved<br />\nthe login information, as it would in a real browser.</p>\n<p>A regular <code>page</code> fixture gives each test a fresh, temporary browser<br />\nsession. This test needs to close and reopen the same saved profile, so it<br />\ncreates persistent browser sessions directly. <code>trace_custom_context</code><br />\nrecords a Playwright trace for those sessions when tracing is enabled.</p>\n<p>Expected result:<br />\n- If Remember Me is off, the customer is logged out after restart.<br />\n- If Remember Me is on, the customer stays logged in after restart.</p>\n<p>Args:<br />\nbrowser_type: Browser engine selected for this test (Chromium, Firefox,<br />\nor WebKit).<br />\nui_base_url: Address of the storefront being tested.<br />\ndynamic_customer: Temporary customer account created for this test.<br />\nThe API fixture also arranges cleanup after the test.<br />\nremember_me: Whether this run checks the Remember Me option.<br />\ntrace_custom_context: Helper that saves traces for failed custom<br />\nbrowser sessions when <code>--tracing retain-on-failure</code> is enabled.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"pytestconfig","time":{"start":1793738907487,"stop":1793738907487,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_session_faker","time":{"start":1793738907488,"stop":1793738907550,"duration":62},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"delete_output_dir","time":{"start":1793738907488,"stop":1793738907488,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0